meta {
  name: f13-6-coverage
  seq: 99
}

docs {
  One success per operation that no other folder covers with a 2xx (D-070, F13.6). Every request reads the
  current versions and ids first, so the folder runs again on the same installation. Requests that need data
  (recommendations, assessments, CIs) skip on an empty installation and fail if `demoMinItems` > 0 (demo data
  loaded); those that need a state the API cannot create (a failed event, a calibration proposal, unmapped
  software) skip when there is none. The role assignment runs last: it revokes the reader's sessions, so this
  folder keeps the highest seq (99) and every folder added later still runs before it with a valid reader token.
}
